    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) headlining our offensive attack. **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost against Abbott, who struggles to neutralize right-handed bats, while **Vinnie Pasquantino** is locked into an ideal spot against Baz, with park factors and platoon advantages pushing his ceiling toward the elite threshold. **Mickey Moniak** (69.68) remains a high-leverage start, particularly due to his speed upside against a slow-working McDonald; the 2% bonus for the stolen base environment cements him as a priority play. Both **James Wood** (64.45) and **Corbin Carroll** (66.61) also project comfortably as strong starts, with **James Wood** specifically thriving on his elite 0.434 xwOBA, which mitigates the moderate difficulty of facing Warren.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Kyle Karros** (46.17) on the bench. While his score hovered in the marginal range, he was ultimately displaced by the higher defensive and situational efficiency of **Austin Riley** and **Isaac Paredes**. We also had to be disciplined with **Josh Naylor**, who sits at 44.64; despite his potential, he is hampered by a difficult matchup against Seymour and limited platoon utility today. Managing our game caps is essential, so we are keeping **Cole Young** and **Zach McKinstry** on the bench, as both fell below our 40-point \"Zebras\" floor for starting viability.\n\nWe are monitoring the risk profile of **Brice Turang** (47.02) closely. While he remains in the lineup, he faces a daunting matchup against Skenes, whose elite arm and efficient release have severely penalized **Brice Turang**\u2019s projected efficiency. Conversely, the aggressive baserunning potential of players like **Mickey Moniak** helps stabilize our output in the scarcity-heavy SB category. With no major weather delays reported, the focus remains on navigating these SP matchups to avoid burning our efficiency reserves on low-ceiling outcomes.",
